# This repository's own file, like README.md: it is NOT synced from the caller.
#
# The caller's .gitignore sits at its repository root, outside every travel prefix, so it
# does not arrive here — and the first `python -m pytest` run in this tree left six
# __pycache__ directories and a .pytest_cache behind, untracked and unignored. That matters
# beyond tidiness: a harness round dispatched from inside this repository needs a clean tree,
# so an unignorable build artefact is a round that cannot start.
#
# Kept minimal on purpose. Anything here should be a by-product this repository's own
# commands produce; editor and OS noise belongs in a personal global ignore file.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Harness runtime state, matching the caller's treatment: the freeze marker
# (.harness/review-pending.json) and the run log are per-checkout, never committed.
.harness/
